{"name":"Stagecoach","hex":"#7f5a44","fetched":"2026-10-13","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"Stagecoach","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Proper noun","definitions":["A census-designated place in Lyon County, Nevada, United States."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/Stagecoach"}],"entries":[{"title":"Stagecoach","blocks":[{"text":"A stagecoach is a four-wheeled public transport coach used to carry paying passengers and light packages on journeys long enough to need a change of horses. It is strongly sprung and generally drawn by four horses although some versions are drawn by six horses."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/0b/Concord_Coach_no._251.jpg/330px-Concord_Coach_no._251.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Stagecoach","wikidata":"Q339249"},{"title":"Stagecoach (1939 film)","blocks":[{"text":"Stagecoach is a 1939 American Western film directed by John Ford and starring Claire Trevor and John Wayne. The screenplay by Dudley Nichols is an adaptation of \"The Stage to Lordsburg\", a 1937 short story by Ernest Haycox. The film follows an eclectic group of travelers riding on a stagecoach through dangerous Apache territory."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/00/Stagecoach_%281939_poster%29.jpg/330px-Stagecoach_%281939_poster%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Stagecoach_(1939_film)","wikidata":"Q50714"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/0b/Concord_Coach_no._251.jpg/500px-Concord_Coach_no._251.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/0b/Concord_Coach_no._251.jpg/1280px-Concord_Coach_no._251.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons